Text:
fearlessMessage is a program that sends one Message to the 'single' manager, and prints the Answer on its standard output.

Grammar:
Message ::= "Show"                                                         \
          | "Show " ProjectName                                         \
          | "Register " Base16                                          \
          | "Quit"                                                      \
          | "Reset"                                                     \
          | "ConnectEclipse " Base16                                    \
          | "EditMetadata " Base16                                      \
          | "OpenWithOrShortcut " Base16                                \
          | "OpenWithOrShortcut " Base16 " " ProjectName " " TypeName   \
          | "Run " ProjectName                                          \
          | "Compile " ProjectName                                      \
          | "Check " ProjectName                                        \
          | "Terminate " ProjectName                                    \
          | "DeleteCache " ProjectName                                  \
          | "Forget " Base16                                            \
          | "Fix " Base16                                               \
          | "Kind " ProjectName " " Kind                                \
          | "Mount " ProjectName " " TypeName " " ProjectName           \
          | "Unmount " ProjectName " " TypeName                         \
          | "Attenuate " ProjectName " " TypeName0 " ".." " TypeNamen   \
          | "SelectMains " ProjectName " " TypeName0 " ".." " TypeNamen
Base16 ::= "Base16:" ([0-9A-F][0-9A-F])+
Answer ::= "Applied\n" Output | "Refused\n" Error
Output ::= the text that the message writes in the Output of its project
Error ::= the text of an error //consistent name

Well formedness:
in Message: all TypeName of a SelectMains are disjoint.
in Base16: second component is a valid OS FS path when decoded.

Invariant:
A Message, as a string, has no unescaped characters, so that "Message" would be recognised as a valid string literal in most settings. This is a direct consequence of the exact syntax.
It is a bug if the exact syntax does not behave like this without the need of any tweaks.

